From bf3bba7c180db293678191f32bcb258ac3c4607d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Wedgwood <cw@f00f.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:20:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] virt-api: accept large identity header sets with Go 1.27

Go 1.27 rejects requests with more than 500 header values by default
(http.Server.MaxHeaderValueCount, golang/go#79936). kube-apiserver
forwards each of a user's groups to aggregated API servers as a
separate X-Remote-Group header, so users with about 500 groups receive
HTTP 431 from virt-api when it is built with Go 1.27.

Set MaxHeaderValueCount to 8192 on the virt-api server for Go 1.27+
builds: 1 MiB at 128 bytes per value. Earlier toolchains use a no-op.

Signed-off-by: Chris Wedgwood <cw@f00f.org>
---
 pkg/virt-api/BUILD.bazel                |  7 ++-
 pkg/virt-api/api.go                     |  1 +
 pkg/virt-api/header_limit_go127.go      | 29 +++++++++++++
 pkg/virt-api/header_limit_go127_test.go | 57 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pkg/virt-api/header_limit_pre_go127.go  | 26 +++++++++++
 5 files changed, 119 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/virt-api/header_limit_go127.go
 create mode 100644 pkg/virt-api/header_limit_go127_test.go
 create mode 100644 pkg/virt-api/header_limit_pre_go127.go

diff --git a/pkg/virt-api/BUILD.bazel b/pkg/virt-api/BUILD.bazel
index 738197de27ae..ea1035f286c1 100644
